ada: heads-up  i'm drafting a small migration + cheatsheet page for dedicated capacity. goal: collect steady/burst/reserved examples, add a short canary rollout checklist, and include tiny SDK snippets (adding a rust example since most pages have js/py/go). will open PR in ~2h. @brian @claire PTAL for anything obvious?

brian: nice. please include a short tf mapping and call out common anchor names so linkcheck doesn't fail. also show one example of label precedence (tenant vs isolation).

claire: +1. can we add a one-liner for ops about SLA wording? folks keep pasting informal language into READMEs.

ada: (typo) ada: meant @claire :)

claire: i can paste the legal-approved blurb. also happy to add the canary checklist bullets: traffic % rollout, monitoring windows, fallback plan.

legal-bot: approved blurb (use verbatim): "Reserved pools are SLA-backed for availability and latency targets. Reactive autoscale policies are best-effort and are not covered by reserved-pool SLAs."

ada: perfect, i'll include that exact sentence. also plan to add a small eviction precedence section: algorithm + worked example so support tickets stop asking "which label wins".

brian: algorithm suggestion: base = isolation_base(isolation_label); if tenant_reserved then final = min(base, tenant_reserved_score) else final = base. worked example: isolation=shared(80) + tenant_reserved_override=10 -> effective=10.

ada: adding that. also including runnable rust snippet (minimal) for create_scale_policy to be different from other pages:

```rust
use redwood_sdk::Client;
use serde_json::json;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let client = Client::new(std::env::var("RW_KEY")?);
  let policy = json!({
    "type": "reactive",
    "targets": { "cpu": 0.8 },
    "burst": { "max_instances": 5, "cooldown": "45s" }
  });
  client.dedicated().create_scale_policy("pool-99", "burst-rust", policy).await?;
  Ok(())
}
```

claire: love the rust example. please also add a tiny tf snippet that uses jsonencode(policy) to avoid HCL pitfalls. mention prefer cooldown as string.

ada: will do. docs-bot: please remind me if linkcheck flags anchors.

